          "file": "frontend/src/hangar/selectionPanel.tsx",
          "line": 62,
          "message": "Unencoded document identifiers can inject query parameters into content requests (OWASP A03:2025 Injection). Encode the identifier and basis values before constructing the request.",
          "confidence": 0.81,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The content controls interpolate documentId and basisId from documentRefs directly into a query string passed to the content reader, without encoding them.",
            "failureScenario": "If an uploaded document produces a documentId such as `case-a/manual.txt&version=99`, clicking Open content passes a request string with an injected version parameter alongside the intended version. The reader may fetch a different document version than the exact evidence tuple shown in the panel."
